      "content": "The concept of a \"liberal order\" is not merely a preference; it is the established moral baseline for international relations, making the protection of human rights and democratic principles a higher moral imperative than absolute sovereignty. Sovereignty is not an absolute right when a state actively plans to commit genocide or undermine global stability through tyranny. Therefore, the defense of universal human dignity, which democracy upholds, supersedes the flawed concept of unchecked national self-determination when that nation becomes a threat.",
      "source": "target",
